MyIAM AI Agent – Weekly Meeting Minutes

RAG / UAT

* The third round of testing has been completed, with more than 70 feedbacks collected in total. Around 39% of the feedback was negative.
* Some of the negative feedback relates to very specific questions that may not necessarily reflect typical end-user needs.
* As Subject Matter Experts, the Support team will review the ~30 negative feedbacks and assess whether each question represents a realistic end-user need.
* Based on this review, we will identify whether the issues are related to gaps in the existing documentation or require further improvements on the RAG side.
* The documentation / Knowledge Base will be updated if needed.
* Based on the outcome, we will decide whether another full round of testing is required or whether targeted testing within the Support team is sufficient.

API Development & AI Agent Integration

* The first batch of APIs – Request Tracking – is ready.
* A service account has already been provided to Innovation Lab. The next step is to confirm that the Innovation Lab developer can successfully access and call the MyIAM APIs using this account.
* A technical discussion can be organized between the Innovation Lab developer and the MyIAM dev team to validate the connection and support the integration.
* If any API adjustments are identified during the AI agent integration, they can be reviewed directly between both development teams and implemented as needed.
* Development of the second batch of APIs has started, with delivery targeted for the end of September.
* Some updates to the second-batch API specifications have already been discussed with Paramesh. The updated points will be confirmed by email.

Next Actions

Action	Owner
Review the ~30 negative feedbacks and assess their relevance to actual end-user needs	Support Team
Identify documentation gaps based on the feedback review	Support Team / Weize
Confirm whether the existing service account can access the MyIAM APIs	Innovation Lab / MyIAM Dev
Organize a technical discussion for API access/integration if needed	Weize
Confirm the agreed updates to the second-batch API specifications	Weize
Continue development of the second API batch	MyIAM Dev Team

有一点我特意没有在 minutes 里写 “39% negative = RAG performance issue”。现在你们还没完成 root-cause analysis，所以正式 minutes 里最好保持中性。等 Support team review 完，你才能进一步区分是 documentation gap / RAG issue / overly specific or out-of-scope question。

